    "https://ucc.peopleadmin.com/postings/12542": {
      "title": "Athletic Information Coordinator",
      "description": "Jobs at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ | Athletic Information Coordinator Skip to Main Content Join our Team and Help Transform our Community… One Student at a Time Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's How to Apply ADA Compliance Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Directions to Campus Foreign Degree Evaluation Athletic Information Coordinator Below you will find the job description for the position including the requirements and any additional documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Job Announcement Position Information Position Title Athletic Information Coordinator Campus Cranford Department Athletics Full-time, Part-time, Adjunct Full Time Exempt or Non-Exempt Exempt Regular,Temporary, or Grant Regular General Description The Athletic Information Coordinator is responsible for overseeing and managing communication, information, and digital media initiatives for the Athletics Department. This includes developing and maintaining athletic websites, producing and distributing electronic newsletters, managing social media campaigns, and ensuring accurate statistical reporting in compliance with NJCAA and institutional standards. In addition, the coordinator supports live event operations by assisting with game management and ensuring that all operational and administrative requirements for home and away contests are executed efficiently. The role plays a key part in promoting the visibility of the athletics program, enhancing fan engagement, and delivering a professional, high-quality experience for student-athletes, coaches, officials, and spectators. The Athletic Information Coordinator works collaboratively with Athletic staff, student workers, and external partners to ensure timely and accurate dissemination of information and seamless execution of digital and live event operations. Characteristics, Duties, and Responsibilities ·         Ensure all information requirements for the Athletics Department are complete, accurate, and compliant with NJCAA , conference, College, and other external organization standards. ·         Manage and maintain all statistical reporting for conference and internal College requirements, ensuring deadlines and compliance standards are consistently met. ·         Submit student-athlete and team awards, honors, and recognitions to relevant governing bodies throughout the academic year. Digital Media and Content Management ·         Update and manage the Athletics Department website, ensuring schedules, rosters, statistics, news, and other relevant content are current and accurate. ·         Manage and update NJCAA Region, conference, and other affiliated athletic websites. ·         Create and coordinate digital content, including text, images, and video, to engage students, fans, and community members, and promote attendance at athletic events. ·         Work collaboratively with College Relations to design and implement digital media campaigns aligned with the mission and goals of the Athletics Department. ·         Develop creative promotions to increase brand awareness, student engagement, and support for athletics programs locally and regionally. ·         Establish and maintain a strong web and social media presence to support student-athlete recruitment and coach recruitment efforts. Media Relations and Publicity ·         Serve as a primary contact and liaison between coaches, student-athletes, and the media for all requests, including interviews, photos, game coverage, broadcast lines, and feature stories. ·         Pitch story ideas for local, regional, and national media outlets, NJCAA , and relevant coaches’ organizations. ·         Prepare, coordinate, and distribute athletic news releases, sport programs, student-athlete feature stories, and game recaps to media outlets. ·         Attend athletic events to produce live-stream content, provide coverage, and create materials for internal and external audiences. Student Engagement and Team Leadership ·         Recruit, train, and manage a team of student writers to produce athletic content for media releases and departmental communications. ·         Solicit student feedback to enhance engagement activities and identify opportunities for new student programs or sports offerings. ·         Design posts and campaigns that sustain audience interest and promote attendance at athletic events. Event and Display Management ·         Aid with coverage and operational support for various internal and external Athletic events. ·         Oversee the Athletics trophy case and displays, ensuring professional presentation and timely updates. ·         Assist in the preparation and distribution of departmental publications in collaboration with UCNJ College Relations and The Union County College Foundation. Other Duties ·         Perform other duties as assigned to support the Athletics Department’s operational and strategic objectives. Education Requirements •\tBachelor’s degree is required. Experience •\tExperience with media productions and marketing of athletic programs through all social media platforms. •\tFirst Aid and CPR certification required, training available. •\tPrevious experience with developing creative promotions. Competencies and Skills Required •\tComputer literate. •\tProven work experience as a social media coordinator. •\tExpertise on multiple social media platforms. •\tAbility to deliver creative content (text, image, and video). •\tAbility to grasp future trends in digital technologies and be proactive. •\tAwareness of, and appreciation for, individual uniqueness and diversity. •\tCommitment to student development, leadership, and teamwork. •\tExcellent oral and written communication skills. •\tAbility to provide a welcoming, inclusive environment for participants. Physical Demands and Work Environment •\tThis position’s duties are normally performed in a typical interior/residence work environment, based on the activity scheduled. •\tThis position’s duties are occasionally performed in an outside work environment, based on the activity scheduled. •\tSome physical effort is required; however, the employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 50 pounds. •\tSome exposure to physical risk. •\tThe employee may be required to walk and sit for extended periods and will be exposed to outside weather conditions; including but not limited to, heat, cold, humidity, rain, and direct sunlight. •\tTravel will be required. Salary $58,000-$60,000 Additional Information UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ is an EEO / AAP Employer/Protected Veteran/Disabled ============== Disclaimer: This job description outlines the general nature and key features performed by various positions that share the same job classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties and qualifications required of all employees assigned to the job. Nothing in this job description restricts management’s right to assign or re-assign duties to this job at any time due to reasonable accommodations or other business reasons. ============== We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes Medical, Dental and Vision Benefits. We also offer twenty vacation days, ten paid holidays, and a ten-week summer work schedule which allows the college to close on Fridays. Other additional benefits include gym privileges, tuition remission for credit and non-credit courses at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ, and tuition reimbursement for an approved degree program at an accredited college or university. Terms of Employment Full Time.  Flexible schedule to meet College needs. Some evening, weekends, and extended hours will be required. Ability and willingness to travel on short notice to all on and off-campus sites as needed by the college.  Employees must establish primary residency in New Jersey within one year of appointment unless an exemption applies. Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/22/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting on UCC.edu Internal Job Posting (Paper Posting) Personal Referral Agency Referral Print Advertisement/Publication (IE: Sunday Star Ledger) Linked-in Facebook NJ.com HigherEdJobs.com HERC.org Other Website Not Listed Other Source Not Listed * If you heard of this employment opportunity from a print advertisement/publication, please indicate where you heard of this employment opportunity.  If you have chosen a specific answer to question number one, please put “N/A” in the answer field. (Open Ended Question) * If you heard of this employment opportunity from another web site or another source not listed in question number one, please indicate where you heard of this employment opportunity.\r\n\r\nIf you have chosen a specific answer to question number one, please put \"N/A\" in the answer field. (Open Ended Question) * Describe a situation when you tried to solve a problem with ideas and methods that had not been tried before.  What was the result? (Open Ended Question) * Describe a specific instance, in a group situation, where you made your views known about an issue important to yourself.  What was the issue, and why was it crucial? (Open Ended Question) * How do you decide which tasks take priority when organizing a complete project? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a valid New Jersey Drivers License? Yes No * Effective September 1, 2011, the “New Jersey First Act” contains new residency requirements for most public officers and employees. \r\nCurrent, new, or prospective public employees should be aware that the New Jersey First Act, N.J.S.A. 52:14-7 (L. 2011, Chapter 70), requires employees of all public employers (for example, state, county, and municipal governments), public agencies, authorities, boards, bodies, commissions, public institutions of higher education, certain quasi-public entities, and all school boards to reside in the State of New Jersey unless otherwise exempted under the law.\r\n\r\nAre you currently a resident of the State of New Jersey? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official due upon hire) Optional Documents UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ Home Student Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
