t of students. •\tIncorporates an appreciation of diverse lifestyles, cultures and national perspectives into courses. •\tAttends scheduled program staff meetings. •\tRepresents the College and Program appropriately to the community. •\tPlans in advance to ensure availability of classroom equipment requisite to successful teaching of assigned tasks •\tAdheres to professional standards of procedures. •\tAdheres to College policies and procedures. Education Requirements •\tCurrent Paramedic Certification or licenses as needed and appropriate and outlined by the NJ State Department of Health. •\tMinimum of High School degree or equivalent required. Experience •\tDemonstrated mastery of subject matter of discipline. •\tTeaching experience preferred. Competencies and Skills Required •\tDemonstrated mastery of subject matter or discipline o\tClinical and/or instructional experience in paramedicine o\tDemonstration of clinical techniques as defined by the paramedic scope of practice Physical Demands and Work Environment •\tThis position’s duties are normally performed in a typical interior/residence work environment, based on the activity scheduled. •\tSome physical effort required; however, the employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 50 pounds. •\tNo or very limited exposure to physical risk. •\tSome travel required. Salary $45.00 per hour Additional Information UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ is an EEO / AAP Employer/Protected Veteran/Disabled ============== Disclaimer: This job description outlines the general nature and key features performed by various positions that share the same job classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties and qualifications required of 