    "https://ucc.peopleadmin.com/postings/12431": {
      "title": "Part-Time Instructor",
      "description": "Jobs at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ | Part-Time Instructor – CompTIA AI Fundamentals Skip to Main Content Join our Team and Help Transform our Community… One Student at a Time Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's How to Apply ADA Compliance Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Directions to Campus Foreign Degree Evaluation Part-Time Instructor – CompTIA AI Fundamentals Below you will find the job description for the position including the requirements and any additional documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Job Announcement Position Information Position Title Part-Time Instructor – CompTIA AI Fundamentals Campus Elizabeth Department Industry-Business Institute Full-time, Part-time, Adjunct Part Time Exempt or Non-Exempt Regular,Temporary, or Grant Regular General Description The Continuing Education & Workforce Development Department seeks a part-time instructor for our 45-hour CompTIA AI Fundamentals certification program. We are looking for an engaging, tech-savvy professional to teach adult learners, career changers, professionals, and job seekers through a blend of in-person sessions and interactive digital modules. You will facilitate learning, monitor progress, and prepare students to earn their official CompTIA AI Fundamentals Competency Certificate (CompCert). Please note that this course covers the practical utilization, prompt engineering, and ethical integration of generative AI tools; advanced machine learning programming, deep data science algorithms, and complex mathematical coding are not part of this curriculum. The 45-hour schedule covers general AI literacy, advanced prompt design, output evaluation, and responsible AI guardrails. Additionally, the curriculum guides students through automating workplace tasks, utilizing AI for research and decision-making, and understanding the core mechanics behind automated AI agents and safety policies. Characteristics, Duties, and Responsibilities •\tProvide CompTIA AI Fundamentals instruction to students utilizing the established curriculum provided by UCNJ Union College, of Union County, NJ. •\tTeach material strictly from the approved CompTIA AI framework, following predefined course modules and delivering a comprehensive, 45-hour pacing syllabus focused on practical tool mastery over software engineering theory. •\tConduct lectures and practical training explicitly aligned with crafting effective prompts, refining machine outputs, and managing digital workflows. •\tProvide quality, technically relevant instruction, assessment, and feedback in both lecture and laboratory settings, utilizing live generative AI tool simulations and auto-graded performance labs. •\tInstruct or co-instruct courses for non-credit programs across traditional lecture, hybrid, and fully online formats, with the ability to teach remote live. •\tMonitor student performance on targeted knowledge checks, motivate active participation, and provide constructive feedback to ensure course standards and digital AI literacy objectives are met. •\tGuide students through core AI workflows, moving seamlessly from basic text generation and data synthesis to multi-step task automation and workspace integration. •\tMaintain meticulous and compliant institutional records, including daily attendance tracking, midterm reporting, and final grade entries. •\tAssist with ongoing course and program evaluations to ensure the training environment effectively prepares non-technical learners for AI-enabled careers. Education Requirements •\tBachelor’s degree in a related field (Information Technology, Business Informatics, Computer Science, or Education) or advanced professional certification from an accredited college or university in a relevant technological discipline is required. •\tOfficial, current CompTIA AI Fundamentals Competency Certificate or equivalent vendor-neutral AI credential preferred Experience •\tRequires a minimum of three (3) or more years of formal teaching experience, preferably instructing adult learners in vocational, corporate training, or non-credit continuing education environments. •\tA minimum of three (3) to five (5) years of practical, professional experience leveraging business technology, information systems, data analytics, or digital workflows where AI optimization tools are actively deployed. •\tAdvanced, demonstrable technical proficiency in prompting and administering primary generative AI platforms (e.g., ChatGPT, Claude, Microsoft Copilot, or Google Gemini). •\tProven track record in adult education, workforce development, corporate training, or vocational instruction. •\tDeep conceptual understanding that the instructional mandate is strictly focused on user applications, workplace efficiency, and human-in-the-loop validation rather than background coding. •\tPractical familiarity with managing course shells within Learning Management Systems (specifically Canvas) and coordinating student activities inside simulated digital laboratory modules (e.g., CompTIA CertMaster Learn/Labs). Competencies and Skills Required •\tSkill in delivering complex technical material strictly according to predefined course outlines and mandatory certificate topics, focusing explicitly on applied operational literacy over theoretical computer science. •\tCurious educator utilizing innovative educational methodologies with the ability to quickly adapt to rapidly changing software capabilities and digital learning management platforms. •\tStrong interpersonal skills to assist leadership with ongoing course evaluations and program improvements. •\tAbility to teach face-to-face, hybrid, and online classrooms using remote-live tools, virtual hands-on exercise environments, video-based lessons, and learning management systems ( LMS ). •\tSkill in evaluating student work, providing actionable feedback, answering software interface inquiries promptly, and motivating active classroom participation. •\tAbility to multi-task in a busy academic environment and effectively pace AI interactive modules to ensure full course completion within the restricted 45-hour programmatic window. Physical Demands and Work Environment •\tThis position’s duties are normally performed in a typical work environment, based on the activity scheduled. •\tSome physical effort required; however, the employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. •\tNo or very limited exposure to physical risk. Salary Additional Information UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ is an EEO / AAP Employer/Protected Veteran/Disabled ============== Disclaimer: This job description outlines the general nature and key features performed by various positions that share the same job classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties and qualifications required of all employees assigned to the job. Nothing in this job description restricts management’s right to assign or re-assign duties to this job at any time due to reasonable accommodations or other business reasons. ============== We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes Medical, Dental and Vision Benefits. We also offer twenty vacation days, ten paid holidays, and a ten-week summer work schedule which allows the college to close on Fridays. Other additional benefits include gym privileges, tuition remission for credit and non-credit courses at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ, and tuition reimbursement for an approved degree program at an accredited college or university. Terms of Employment Part-time (Hired on a project basis. Assignment Contract) Part Time, course specific. CEWD courses can be held at campus locations in Elizabeth Cranford, or Plainfield. Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/08/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting on UCC.edu Internal Job Posting (Paper Posting) Personal Referral Agency Referral Print Advertisement/Publication (IE: Sunday Star Ledger) Linked-in Facebook NJ.com HigherEdJobs.com HERC.org Other Website Not Listed Other Source Not Listed If you heard of this employment opportunity from a print advertisement/publication, please indicate where you heard of this employment opportunity.  If you have chosen a specific answer to question number one, please put “N/A” in the answer field. (Open Ended Question) If you heard of this employment opportunity from another web site or another source not listed in question number one, please indicate where you heard of this employment opportunity.\r\n\r\nIf you have chosen a specific answer to question number one, please put \"N/A\" in the answer field. (Open Ended Question) Describe a situation when you tried to solve a problem with ideas and methods that had not been tried before.  What was the result? (Open Ended Question) Describe a specific instance, in a group situation, where you made your views known about an issue important to yourself.  What was the issue, and why was it crucial? (Open Ended Question) How do you decide which tasks take priority when organizing a complete project? (Open Ended Question) Do you have a valid New Jersey Drivers License? Yes No Effective September 1, 2011, the “New Jersey First Act” contains new residency requirements for most public officers and employees. \r\nCurrent, new, or prospective public employees should be aware that the New Jersey First Act, N.J.S.A. 52:14-7 (L. 2011, Chapter 70), requires employees of all public employers (for example, state, county, and municipal governments), public agencies, authorities, boards, bodies, commissions, public institutions of higher education, certain quasi-public entities, and all school boards to reside in the State of New Jersey unless otherwise exempted under the law.\r\n\r\nAre you currently a resident of the State of New Jersey? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official due upon hire) Optional Documents UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ Home Student Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
