      "title": "Jobs at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ",
      "description": "Jobs at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ | Part-time Librarian Skip to Main Content Join our Team and Help Transform our Community… One Student at a Time Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's How to Apply ADA Compliance Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Directions to Campus Foreign Degree Evaluation Part-time Librarian Below you will find the job description for the position including the requirements and any additional documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Job Announcement Position Information Position Title Part-time Librarian Campus All Campuses Department Libraries Full-time, Part-time, Adjunct Part Time Exempt or Non-Exempt Non-Exempt Regular,Temporary, or Grant Regular General Description The Part-time Librarian fosters a supportive and informative learning space for students, faculty, and staff at UCNJ . The Part-time Librarian provides essential reference and research assistance and helps students use the information resources available at the College. Additionally, the Part-time Librarian contributes to library programming and projects. Characteristics, Duties, and Responsibilities •\tProvides research and reference assistance to students, faculty, and staff. •\tAssists faculty, staff, and students with locating and retrieving information through the use of library databases and resources. •\tDevelops information literacy within the UCNJ community through guidance on effective and ethical use of online and AI tools. •\tCollaborates with Librarians and other faculty to provide in-class Library Instruction. •\tMaintains statistics of library services rendered while on duty. •\tAssists with special projects and programs, as needed. •\tPerforms other duties as assigned by the Director of Libraries or designee. Education Requirements •\tAmerican Library Association accredited MLS degree required. Experience •\tAcademic Library experience strongly preferred. Competencies and Skills Required •\tStrong interpersonal and communication skills. •\tStrong reference experience. •\tStrong Library instruction and/or teaching experience. •\tCuriosity •\tQuick study •\tKnowledge of electronic outreach for libraries. •\tCommitment to a culturally diverse perspective. •\tExcellent oral and written communication skills. •\tKnowledge of computer applications in library and office environment. •\tExperience with Windows applications. Physical Demands and Work Environment •\tThis position’s duties are normally performed in a typical interior/residence work environment, based on the activity scheduled. •\tSome physical effort required; however, the employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. •\tNo or very limited exposure to physical risk. •\tSome travel required. Salary $32.00 per hour Additional Information UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ is an EEO / AAP Employer/Protected Veteran/Disabled ============== Disclaimer: This job description outlines the general nature and key features performed by various positions that share the same job classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties and qualifications required of all employees assigned to the job. Nothing in this job description restricts management’s right to assign or re-assign duties to this job at any time due to reasonable accommodations or 