    "https://ucc.peopleadmin.com/postings/12432": {
      "title": "Part-Time Instructor",
      "description": "Jobs at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ | Part-Time Instructor - Intuit QuickBooks Certified User (QBOCU) Certification  Program Skip to Main Content Join our Team and Help Transform our Community… One Student at a Time Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's How to Apply ADA Compliance Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Directions to Campus Foreign Degree Evaluation Part-Time Instructor - Intuit QuickBooks Certified User (QBOCU) Certification  Program Below you will find the job description for the position including the requirements and any additional documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Job Announcement Position Information Position Title Part-Time Instructor - Intuit QuickBooks Certified User (QBOCU) Certification  Program Campus Elizabeth Department Industry-Business Institute Full-time, Part-time, Adjunct Part Time Exempt or Non-Exempt Non-Exempt Regular,Temporary, or Grant Regular General Description The Continuing Education & Workforce Development Department seeks a part-time instructor for our Intuit QuickBooks Certified User certification program. We are looking for an engaging, tech-savvy professional to teach adult learners, career changers, entrepreneurs, and job seekers through a blend of in-person sessions and on-demand online modules. You will facilitate learning, monitor progress, and prepare students to pass the official Certiport Intuit QuickBooks Online Certified User exam. Please note that this course exclusively covers the practical functionality of the QuickBooks software; foundational accounting and bookkeeping principles are not part of the curriculum. The curriculum focuses on QuickBooks Online administration, company file setup, user permissions, contact list management, and constructing customized product and service lists for tracking inventory. Additionally, students will master “Money-In” workflows (estimates, invoices, sales receipts, payments) and “Money-Out” workflows (checks, bills, credit cards, purchase orders), as well as bank feeds, automated bank rules, receipt uploads, and generating core financial reports like Profit and Loss statements, Balance Sheets, and Audit Logs. Prepares the student for employment careers in accounting, bookkeeping, finance, and financial administration. This is a part-time position and reports to the Program Director. Characteristics, Duties, and Responsibilities • Provide QBCU instruction to students utilizing the established curriculum provided by UCNJ Union College, of Union County, NJ for the QuickBooks Certified User ( QBCU ) Certification Program. • Teach material strictly from the approved curriculum, following predefined course outlines and delivering a clear, comprehensive syllabus focused solely on software functionality rather than foundational accounting principles. • Conduct lectures and practical training explicitly aligned with navigating the digital workspace and passing the official QuickBooks Certified User Certification Exam. • Provide quality, technically relevant instruction, assessment, and feedback in both lecture and laboratory settings, utilizing real-world simulations, hands-on exercise labs, and project workbooks. • Instruct or co-instruct courses for non-credit programs across traditional lecture, hybrid, and fully online formats, with the ability to teach remote live and support asynchronous on-demand modules. • Monitor student performance on targeted pre-and post-assessments, motivate active participation, and provide constructive feedback to ensure course standards and software fluency objectives are met. • Guide students through core software workflows, including contact and inventory list management, income and expense tracking, and client invoicing automation. • Maintain meticulous and compliant institutional records, including daily attendance tracking, midterm reporting, and final grade entries. • Assist with ongoing course and program evaluations to ensure the curriculum continuously prepares students for the official online testing window. Education Requirements • Bachelor’s degree in a related field or advanced certification from a four-year college or university in the relevant industry/discipline is required. • Official QuickBooks Certified User ( QBCU ) Certification or QuickBooks Certified ProAdvisor designation preferred. Experience • Requires a minimum of 3+ years instructional experience. • A minimum of five (5) years’ experience in accounting, finance, and/or financial administration. • Software Expertise: Advanced, demonstrable proficiency in cloud-based accounting software (QuickBooks Online preferred). • Proven experience in adult education, corporate training, or vocational instruction. • QuickBooks Certified User or equivalent ProAdvisor certification is highly preferred. • Exceptional ability to translate complex digital procedures into easy-to-understand, actionable lessons. • Deep understanding that the focus is on software navigation and application, rather than teaching core bookkeeping theory. • Learning Management Systems (Canvas) and Simulated Learning Environments. Competencies and Skills Required • Skill in delivering complex technical material strictly according to predefined course outlines, institutional syllabi, and mandatory certification topics, focusing explicitly on software functionality over theoretical accounting principles. • Curious educator utilizing innovative educational methodologies with the ability to quickly master new program curricula and digital learning management platforms. • Strong interpersonal skills to assist leadership with ongoing course evaluations and program improvements. • Mastery of cloud-based accounting workflows, digital workspaces, automated invoicing, expense tracking, and the specific software navigation skills tested on the official certification exam. • Ability to teach face-to-face, hybrid, and online classrooms using remote-live tools, virtual hands-on exercise labs, video-based lessons, and learning management systems ( LMS ). • Skill in evaluating student work via pre- and post-assessments, providing actionable feedback, answering software-related inquiries promptly, and motivating active classroom participation. • Ability to multi-task in a busy academic environment and effectively pace software simulations and lectures to ensure full classroom testing readiness within an accelerated curriculum window. Physical Demands and Work Environment • This position’s duties are normally performed in a typical work environment, based on the activity scheduled. • Some physical effort required; however, the employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. • No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Salary Additional Information UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ is an EEO / AAP Employer/Protected Veteran/Disabled ============== Disclaimer: This job description outlines the general nature and key features performed by various positions that share the same job classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties and qualifications required of all employees assigned to the job. Nothing in this job description restricts management’s right to assign or re-assign duties to this job at any time due to reasonable accommodations or other business reasons. ============== We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes Medical, Dental and Vision Benefits. We also offer twenty vacation days, ten paid holidays, and a ten-week summer work schedule which allows the college to close on Fridays. Other additional benefits include gym privileges, tuition remission for credit and non-credit courses at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ, and tuition reimbursement for an approved degree program at an accredited college or university. Terms of Employment Part-time (Hired on a project basis. Assignment Contract) Part Time, course specific. CEWD courses can be held at campus locations in Elizabeth Cranford, or Plainfield. Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/09/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting on UCC.edu Internal Job Posting (Paper Posting) Personal Referral Agency Referral Print Advertisement/Publication (IE: Sunday Star Ledger) Linked-in Facebook NJ.com HigherEdJobs.com HERC.org Other Website Not Listed Other Source Not Listed If you heard of this employment opportunity from a print advertisement/publication, please indicate where you heard of this employment opportunity.  If you have chosen a specific answer to question number one, please put “N/A” in the answer field. (Open Ended Question) If you heard of this employment opportunity from another web site or another source not listed in question number one, please indicate where you heard of this employment opportunity.\r\n\r\nIf you have chosen a specific answer to question number one, please put \"N/A\" in the answer field. (Open Ended Question) Describe a situation when you tried to solve a problem with ideas and methods that had not been tried before.  What was the result? (Open Ended Question) Describe a specific instance, in a group situation, where you made your views known about an issue important to yourself.  What was the issue, and why was it crucial? (Open Ended Question) How do you decide which tasks take priority when organizing a complete project? (Open Ended Question) Do you have a valid New Jersey Drivers License? Yes No Effective September 1, 2011, the “New Jersey First Act” contains new residency requirements for most public officers and employees. \r\nCurrent, new, or prospective public employees should be aware that the New Jersey First Act, N.J.S.A. 52:14-7 (L. 2011, Chapter 70), requires employees of all public employers (for example, state, county, and municipal governments), public agencies, authorities, boards, bodies, commissions, public institutions of higher education, certain quasi-public entities, and all school boards to reside in the State of New Jersey unless otherwise exempted under the law.\r\n\r\nAre you currently a resident of the State of New Jersey? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official due upon hire) Optional Documents UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ Home Student Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ucc.peopleadmin.com/postings/12348": {
      "title": "Part Time Industry-Business Institute (IBI) Instructor Pool",
      "description": "Jobs at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ | Part Time Industry-Business Institute (IBI) Instructor Pool Skip to Main Content Join our Team and Help Transform our Community… One Student at a Time Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's How to Apply ADA Compliance Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Directions to Campus Foreign Degree Evaluation Part Time Industry-Business Institute (IBI) Instructor Pool Below you will find the job description for the position including the requirements and any additional documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Job Announcement Position Information Position Title Part Time Industry-Business Institute (IBI) Instructor Pool Campus Cranford, Elizabeth, Plainfield, and other off campus locations as needed Department Industry-Business Institute Full-time, Part-time, Adjunct Part Time Exempt or Non-Exempt Non-Exempt Regular,Temporary, or Grant Temporary General Description Instructors needed to teach the following classes for Industry-Business Institute clients: Characteristics, Duties, and Responsibilities 1. English as a Second Language (Level 1, Level 2, Level 3) 2. Microsoft Office Instructors (Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Access, Outlook and Project). 3. Supply Chain Management 4. Workplace Readiness Instructors (Verbal Communication Skills, Written Communication Skills, Customer Service, Team Building, Time Management, Problem Solving) Education Requirements Bachelor’s Degrees required. Master’s Degrees preferred. Experience • Teaching experience preferred. • Flexible schedule. • Working with a diverse population. Competencies and Skills Required Background experience in teaching the IBI courses listed above. Physical Demands and Work Environment • This position’s duties are normally performed in a typical interior/residence work environment, based on the activity scheduled. • Some physical effort required; however, the employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. • No or very limited exposure to physical risk. • Some travel required. Salary Additional Information UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ is an EEO / AAP Employer/Protected Veteran/Disabled ====== Disclaimer: This job description outlines the general nature and key features performed by various positions that share the same job classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties and qualifications required of all employees assigned to the job. Nothing in this job description restricts management’s right to assign or re-assign duties to this job at any time due to reasonable accommodations or other business reasons. Terms of Employment Industry-Business Institute courses will be held at client locations and the Cranford, Elizabeth, and Plainfield campuses. Must be available during weekdays. Weekend and evening opportunities may occur. Posting Detail Information Open Date 05/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting on UCC.edu Internal Job Posting (Paper Posting) Personal Referral Agency Referral Print Advertisement/Publication (IE: Sunday Star Ledger) Linked-in Facebook NJ.com HigherEdJobs.com HERC.org Other Website Not Listed Other Source Not Listed * If you heard of