    "https://ucc.peopleadmin.com/postings/12434": {
      "title": "Part-Time Instructor",
      "description": "Jobs at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ | Part-Time Instructor – Microsoft Excel 365 (Associate &amp; Expert) Certification Programs Skip to Main Content Join our Team and Help Transform our Community… One Student at a Time Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's How to Apply ADA Compliance Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Directions to Campus Foreign Degree Evaluation Part-Time Instructor – Microsoft Excel 365 (Associate & Expert) Certification Programs Below you will find the job description for the position including the requirements and any additional documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Job Announcement Position Information Position Title Part-Time Instructor – Microsoft Excel 365 (Associate & Expert) Certification Programs Campus Elizabeth Department Industry-Business Institute Full-time, Part-time, Adjunct Part Time Exempt or Non-Exempt Non-Exempt Regular,Temporary, or Grant Regular General Description The Continuing Education & Workforce Development Department seeks a part-time instructor for our Microsoft Excel 365 Associate and Expert certification programs. We are looking for an engaging, tech-savvy professional to teach adult learners, career changers, entrepreneurs, and job seekers through a blend of in-person sessions and on-demand online modules. Reporting to the Program Director, you will facilitate learning, monitor progress, and prepare students to pass the official Certiport Microsoft Excel 365 Associate (MO-210) and Expert (MO-211) exams. Please note that this course exclusively covers the practical functionality, tools, and syntax of Excel software; foundational mathematical theory or statistical principles are not part of the curriculum. At the Associate level, the curriculum focuses on managing worksheets, creating cells and ranges, formatting tables, applying basic formulas and functions, and generating charts. Expert-level topics expand into managing advanced workbook options, restricting user access, formatting custom data layouts, and deploying advanced formulas, including logical, financial, and lookups. Additionally, the curriculum guides students through advanced data analysis, which includes managing PivotTables, configuring Pivot Charts, and creating interactive dashboards. Characteristics, Duties, and Responsibilities • Provide Excel 365 Level 1, Level 2, Level 3 instruction to students utilizing the established curriculum provided by UCNJ Union College, of Union County, NJ for both the Excel Associate and Excel Expert Certification Programs. • Teach material strictly from the approved curriculum, following predefined course outlines and delivering a clear, comprehensive syllabus focused solely on software functionality and formula syntax. • Conduct lectures and practical training explicitly aligned with navigating the digital workspace and passing the official Microsoft Office Specialist Excel Associate and Expert Exams. • Provide quality, technically relevant instruction, assessment, and feedback in both lecture and laboratory settings, utilizing real-world simulations, hands-on exercise labs, and project workbooks. • Instruct or co-instruct courses for non-credit programs across traditional lecture, hybrid, and fully online formats, with the ability to teach remote live and support asynchronous on-demand modules. • Monitor student performance on targeted pre-and post-assessments, motivate active participation, and provide constructive feedback to ensure course standards and data fluency objectives are met. • Guide students through core and advanced software workflows, moving seamlessly from basic cell formatting to advanced nesting functions, macro utilization, and data modeling. • Maintain meticulous and compliant institutional records, including daily attendance tracking, midterm reporting, and final grade entries. • Assist with ongoing course and program evaluations to ensure the curriculum continuously prepares students for the official online testing windows. Education Requirements • Bachelor’s degree in a related field or advanced certification from a four-year college or university in the relevant industry/discipline is required. • Official Microsoft Office Specialist ( MOS ) Excel 365 Associate and Expert Certifications (or Microsoft Office Specialist: Excel Expert Master designation) preferred. Experience • Requires a minimum of three (3) or more years of formal teaching experience, preferably instructing adult learners in vocational or non-credit continuing education environments. • A minimum of five (5) years of practical, hands-on experience in data analysis, business intelligence, finance, or administrative management roles heavily utilizing advanced spreadsheets. • Advanced, demonstrable technical proficiency in Microsoft Excel 365, specifically including PivotTables, Power Query, dynamic arrays, and complex nested functions. • Proven track record in adult education, workforce development, corporate training, or vocational instruction. • Official Microsoft Office Specialist: Excel Associate (MO-210) AND Excel Expert (MO-211) certifications are highly preferred. • Exceptional communication skills with a proven ability to translate complex formula syntax, data modeling logic, and error troubleshooting into clear, actionable lessons. • Deep conceptual understanding that the instructional mandate is strictly focused on software tool functionality, formula syntax, and interface navigation rather than teaching foundational mathematical or statistical theory. • Practical familiarity with managing course shells within Learning Management Systems (specifically Canvas) and coordinating student activities inside simulated digital learning environments (e.g., GMetrix) Competencies and Skills Required • Skill in delivering complex technical material strictly according to predefined course outlines, institutional syllabi, and mandatory certification topics, focusing explicitly on software functionality over theoretical mathematical or statistical principles. • Curious educator utilizing innovative educational methodologies with the ability to quickly master new program curricula and digital learning management platforms. • Strong interpersonal skills to assist leadership with ongoing course evaluations and program improvements. • Mastery of Excel 365 spreadsheet workflows, user interface navigation, advanced formula syntax, data visualization, and the specific advanced analytical skills tested on both the Associate and Expert certification exams. • Ability to teach face-to-face, hybrid, and online classrooms using remote-live tools, virtual hands-on exercise labs, video-based lessons, and learning management systems ( LMS ). • Skill in evaluating student work via pre- and post-assessments, providing actionable feedback, answering software-related syntax inquiries promptly, and motivating active classroom participation. • Ability to multi-task in a busy academic environment and effectively pace software simulations, exercises, and lectures to ensure full classroom testing readiness within an accelerated curriculum window. Physical Demands and Work Environment • This position’s duties are normally performed in a typical work environment, based on the activity scheduled. • Some physical effort required; however, the employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. • No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Salary Additional Information UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ is an EEO / AAP Employer/Protected Veteran/Disabled ============== Disclaimer: This job description outlines the general nature and key features performed by various positions that share the same job classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties and qualifications required of all employees assigned to the job. Nothing in this job description restricts management’s right to assign or re-assign duties to this job at any time due to reasonable accommodations or other business reasons. ============== We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes Medical, Dental and Vision Benefits. We also offer twenty vacation days, ten paid holidays, and a ten-week summer work schedule which allows the college to close on Fridays. Other additional benefits include gym privileges, tuition remission for credit and non-credit courses at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ, and tuition reimbursement for an approved degree program at an accredited college or university. Terms of Employment Part-time (Hired on a project basis. Assignment Contract) Part Time, course specific. CEWD courses can be held at campus locations in Elizabeth Cranford, or Plainfield. Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/09/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting on UCC.edu Internal Job Posting (Paper Posting) Personal Referral Agency Referral Print Advertisement/Publication (IE: Sunday Star Ledger) Linked-in Facebook NJ.com HigherEdJobs.com HERC.org Other Website Not Listed Other Source Not Listed If you heard of this employment opportunity from a print advertisement/publication, please indicate where you heard of this employment opportunity.  If you have chosen a specific answer to question number one, please put “N/A” in the answer field. (Open Ended Question) If you heard of this employment opportunity from another web site or another source not listed in question number one, please indicate where you heard of this employment opportunity.\r\n\r\nIf you have chosen a specific answer to question number one, please put \"N/A\" in the answer field. (Open Ended Question) Describe a situation when you tried to solve a problem with ideas and methods that had not been tried before.  What was the result? (Open Ended Question) Describe a specific instance, in a group situation, where you made your views known about an issue important to yourself.  What was the issue, and why was it crucial? (Open Ended Question) How do you decide which tasks take priority when organizing a complete project? (Open Ended Question) Do you have a valid New Jersey Drivers License? Yes No Effective September 1, 2011, the “New Jersey First Act” contains new residency requirements for most public officers and employees. \r\nCurrent, new, or prospective public employees should be aware that the New Jersey First Act, N.J.S.A. 52:14-7 (L. 2011, Chapter 70), requires employees of all public employers (for example, state, county, and municipal governments), public agencies, authorities, boards, bodies, commissions, public institutions of higher education, certain quasi-public entities, and all school boards to reside in the State of New Jersey unless otherwise exempted under the law.\r\n\r\nAre you currently a resident of the State of New Jersey? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official due upon hire) Optional Documents UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ Home Student Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
