    "https://ucc.peopleadmin.com/postings/12438": {
      "title": "Part-Time Instructor",
      "description": "Jobs at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ | Part-Time Instructor – CompTIA A+ Certification (V15 Core 1 and V15 Core 2) Skip to Main Content Join our Team and Help Transform our Community… One Student at a Time Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's How to Apply ADA Compliance Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Directions to Campus Foreign Degree Evaluation Part-Time Instructor – CompTIA A+ Certification (V15 Core 1 and V15 Core 2) Below you will find the job description for the position including the requirements and any additional documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Job Announcement Position Information Position Title Part-Time Instructor – CompTIA A+ Certification (V15 Core 1 and V15 Core 2) Campus Elizabeth Department Industry-Business Institute Full-time, Part-time, Adjunct Part Time Exempt or Non-Exempt Non-Exempt Regular,Temporary, or Grant Regular General Description The Continuing Education & Workforce Development Department seeks a part-time instructor for our CompTIA A+ Certification program. We are looking for an engaging, tech-savvy professional to teach adult learners, entrepreneurs, career changers, and job seekers through a blend of in-person sessions and on-demand online modules. You will facilitate learning, monitor progress, and prepare students to pass both the official CompTIA A+ V15 Core 1 and V15 Core 2 exams. Please note that this course covers the practical operational functionality, troubleshooting procedures, and configuration setups tested on the exams; theoretical computer science mathematics or abstract engineering principles are not part of the curriculum. Under Core 1, the curriculum focuses on mobile devices, networking technology, hardware components, virtualization, cloud computing, and network troubleshooting. Core 2 topics expand into installing and configuring operating systems (Windows, Mac, Linux, Android, iOS), expanded security parameters, software troubleshooting, and operational procedures. Additionally, the curriculum guides students through standard help desk ticket resolution, malware remediation, and security script basics. Characteristics, Duties, and Responsibilities • Provide CompTIA A+ instruction to students utilizing the established curriculum provided by UCNJ Union College, of Union County, NJ for both the Core 1 and Core 2 Certification Programs. • Teach material strictly from the approved curriculum, following predefined course outlines and delivering a clear, comprehensive syllabus focused solely on hardware/software functionality and troubleshooting workflows. • Conduct lectures and practical training explicitly aligned with navigating command-line interfaces, physical hardware assemblies, and passing the official CompTIA A+ certification exams. • Provide quality, technically relevant instruction, assessment, and feedback in both lecture and laboratory settings, utilizing real-world simulations, hands-on exercise labs, and project workbooks. • Instruct or co-instruct courses for non-credit programs across traditional lecture, hybrid, and fully online formats, with the ability to teach remote live and support asynchronous on-demand modules. • Monitor student performance on targeted pre-and post-assessments, motivate active participation, and provide constructive feedback to ensure course standards and technical fluency objectives are met. • Guide students through core and advanced IT workflows, moving seamlessly from basic computer component assembly to advanced network configuration, malware removal, and security policy management. • Maintain meticulous and compliant institutional records, including daily attendance tracking, midterm reporting, and final grade entries. • Assist with ongoing course and program evaluations to ensure the curriculum continuously prepares students for the official testing windows. Education Requirements • Bachelor’s degree in a related field or advanced certification from a four-year college or university in the relevant industry/discipline is required. • Official, current CompTIA A+ Certification (covering both Core 1 and Core 2 domains) preferred. Experience • Requires a minimum of three (3) or more years of formal teaching experience, preferably instructing adult learners in vocational or non-credit continuing education environments. • A minimum of five (5) years of practical, hands-on experience in desktop support, network administration, systems troubleshooting, or corporate help desk engineering roles. • Advanced, demonstrable technical proficiency in PC hardware customization, network router configuration, enterprise malware removal tools, and navigating active directory environments. • Proven track record in adult education, workforce development, corporate training, or vocational instruction. • Official, active CompTIA A+ certification is required. Higher-level certifications (such as CompTIA Network+, Security+, or Cisco CCNA ) are highly preferred. • Exceptional communication skills with a proven ability to translate complex networking topologies, Command Prompt syntax, and hardware configurations into clear, actionable lessons. • Deep conceptual understanding that the instructional mandate is strictly focused on device management, configuration workflows, and physical diagnostics rather than theoretical computing architecture. • Practical familiarity with managing course shells within Learning Management Systems (specifically Canvas) and coordinating student activities inside simulated digital laboratory environments (e.g., CompTIA CertMaster Labs). Competencies and Skills Required • Skill in delivering complex technical material strictly according to predefined course outlines, institutional syllabi, and mandatory certification topics, focusing explicitly on applied technical functionality over abstract computer science theories. • Ability to multi-task in a busy academic environment and effectively pace hardware simulations, live diagnostics, and lectures to ensure full classroom testing readiness within an accelerated curriculum window. • Curious educator utilizing innovative educational methodologies with the ability to quickly master new program curricula and digital learning management platforms. • Strong interpersonal skills to assist leadership with ongoing course evaluations and program improvements. • Ability to teach face-to-face, hybrid, and online classrooms using remote-live tools, virtual hands-on exercise labs, video-based lessons, and learning management systems ( LMS ). • Skill in evaluating student work via pre-and post-assessments, providing actionable feedback, answering hardware or software configuration inquiries promptly, and motivating active classroom participation. Physical Demands and Work Environment • This position’s duties are normally performed in a typical work environment, based on the activity scheduled. • Some physical effort required; however, the employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. • No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Salary Additional Information UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ is an EEO / AAP Employer/Protected Veteran/Disabled ============== Disclaimer: This job description outlines the general nature and key features performed by various positions that share the same job classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties and qualifications required of all employees assigned to the job. Nothing in this job description restricts management’s right to assign or re-assign duties to this job at any time due to reasonable accommodations or other business reasons. ============== We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes Medical, Dental and Vision Benefits. We also offer twenty vacation days, ten paid holidays, and a ten-week summer work schedule which allows the college to close on Fridays. Other additional benefits include gym privileges, tuition remission for credit and non-credit courses at UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ, and tuition reimbursement for an approved degree program at an accredited college or university. Terms of Employment Part-time (Hired on a project basis. Assignment Contract) Part Time, course specific. CEWD courses can be held at campus locations in Elizabeth Cranford, or Plainfield. Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/08/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting on UCC.edu Internal Job Posting (Paper Posting) Personal Referral Agency Referral Print Advertisement/Publication (IE: Sunday Star Ledger) Linked-in Facebook NJ.com HigherEdJobs.com HERC.org Other Website Not Listed Other Source Not Listed If you heard of this employment opportunity from a print advertisement/publication, please indicate where you heard of this employment opportunity.  If you have chosen a specific answer to question number one, please put “N/A” in the answer field. (Open Ended Question) Describe a situation when you tried to solve a problem with ideas and methods that had not been tried before.  What was the result? (Open Ended Question) If you heard of this employment opportunity from another web site or another source not listed in question number one, please indicate where you heard of this employment opportunity.\r\n\r\nIf you have chosen a specific answer to question number one, please put \"N/A\" in the answer field. (Open Ended Question) Describe a specific instance, in a group situation, where you made your views known about an issue important to yourself.  What was the issue, and why was it crucial? (Open Ended Question) How do you decide which tasks take priority when organizing a complete project? (Open Ended Question) Do you have a valid New Jersey Drivers License? Yes No Effective September 1, 2011, the “New Jersey First Act” contains new residency requirements for most public officers and employees. \r\nCurrent, new, or prospective public employees should be aware that the New Jersey First Act, N.J.S.A. 52:14-7 (L. 2011, Chapter 70), requires employees of all public employers (for example, state, county, and municipal governments), public agencies, authorities, boards, bodies, commissions, public institutions of higher education, certain quasi-public entities, and all school boards to reside in the State of New Jersey unless otherwise exempted under the law.\r\n\r\nAre you currently a resident of the State of New Jersey? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official due upon hire) Optional Documents UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination, as required by state and/or federal law, in all programs and activities, including employment and access to its career and technical programs. UCNJ Union College of Union County, NJ Home Student Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
